BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Soup with Chef Erika Yochum
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261122T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261122T150000
UID:182b8753077123d071b5c1264930847b@wfhb.org
DESCRIPTION:With colder temperatures comes a need for warm and nourishing 
 food. Soups\, as a culinary category\, offer such a range of textures\, in
 gredients and flavors. Whether it’s blended\, vegetarian\, with or witho
 ut grains\, loaded with greens or even super creamy and cheesy\, soup is a
  delicious staple across cultures. Chef Erika is visiting today to walk yo
 u through two recipes of her own creation and teach you what principles sh
 e uses when building a soup recipe from scratch. She’ll discuss how to p
 repare broth from scratch and how to select aromatics that pair well.  De
 mo style class with Erika. You’ll eat soup at the end! As Erika has a kn
 ack for bringing treats to her classes\, we recommend considering this you
 r afternoon meal. We encourage you to sign up for classes online. When you
  register online\, you’ll also pay online. While we will accept walk-ins
  before class if capacity allows\, registering ahead of time secures your 
 spot and creates a more seamless class experience.
LOCATION:In the Kitchen\, 115 N College Ave\, Suite 014\, Bloomington (For
  your convenience\, we recommend using the Uptown Plaza alley entrance bet
 ween JL Waters and Peach Cobbler Factory).
URL:https://wfhb.org/events/soup-with-chef-erika-yochum/
X-SOURCE:WFHB Community Calendar
END:VEVENT
