BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Full Moon Hike
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261125T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261125T203000
UID:4e9f70bc9b16afc53bc486973e0417ed@wfhb.org
DESCRIPTION:Join a park naturalist for a guided night hike around Lake Ogl
 e! The Full Moon is the brightest night of the month\, leading to excellen
 t views of the lake. Learn about November’s full moon\, the Beaver Moon.
  Trail 7 is rated moderate\, but should be considered rugged in the dark. 
 The trail has some staircases\, uneven surfaces\, and muddy spots. It is 1
 .2 miles and will take about an hour and a half to complete. Please do not
  bring pets on night hikes. Red flashlights are preferred for night vision
  and can be loaned to hikers on request.
LOCATION:Brown County State Park\, Lake Ogle Parking Lot\, 1405 S.R. 46 W
 \, Nashville\, IN
URL:https://wfhb.org/events/full-moon-hike-2/
X-SOURCE:WFHB Community Calendar
END:VEVENT
